# WISE (Malinowski, Allcock and Ballance, arXiv:2305.12773), as the team's transport deck writes
# it for QCCD Studio: a chip of cells, one junction zone and h gate zones each, sorted by parallel
# switched swaps, with one kind of operation running across the chip in a step.
#
# W1-W6, W10 and W11 are the deck's S1-S6, S10 and S11 where no R rule says the same thing.  The
# deck's S7 is an algorithm and S12 says what switching does not cost, so neither is a rule; S8's
# R2 and R23 and S9's R6, R6b and R12 are in the list below.

ruleset "wise"
title "WISE's rules"
about "A chip of cells, one junction zone and h gate zones each. A zone holds one qubit, or two for a gate or in the middle of a swap. A swap step plays one kind of pair at one parity, one direction to a half; one kind of operation runs across the chip in a step; a layer of gates is one gate at one angle; and every layer pays for its shims before it starts. No ion rests on a junction zone, which holds at most one at a time."

use R0, R1, R2, R3, R4, R4b, R4d, R5, R6, R6b, R7, R7c, R8, R11, R12, R13, R14, R15, R16, R17
use R18, R19, R20, R21, R22, R23, R24, R25

param max_chain = 2
use W1, W2, W4, W10, W11
